        "original_id": "5b155044-cdbe-5ee1-b56a-6e968c156ea4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Jefferson, George Cuvier, Daniel Boone, Benjamin Franklin, William Henry Harrison, George Washington\n- Places: United States, Jefferson County, Oklahoma, Great Britain, France\n- Roles: American Founding Father, President of the United States\n- Concepts: democracy, republicanism, individual rights, Declaration of Independence, statehood, paleontology\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Jefferson was born on April 13, 1743, and died on July 4, 1826.\n- Thomas Jefferson was an American Founding Father and the principal author of the Declaration of Independence.\n- Thomas Jefferson advocated democracy, republicanism, and individual rights, helping motivate American colonists to break from Great Britain and form a new nation.\n- Thomas Jefferson produced formative documents and decisions at both the state and national level.\n- Thomas Jefferson served as the third President of the United States from 1801 to 1809.\n- Fossils in the United States were studied by George Cuvier, Daniel Boone, Benjamin Franklin, William Henry Harrison, Thomas Jefferson, and George Washington.\n- Jefferson County in Oklahoma was created at statehood and named in honor of President Thomas Jefferson.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
